## Step 2 — New Measures to Create

### 2a — Male measures (check your data first)

Before creating these, verify the columns exist in `fact_acs_wi_county`.
Open the table in Power Query or Data view and check for:
- A male labor force participation column/row
- A male population share column/row

If the data is there, create these on `fact_acs_wi_county`:

**`(IND) Men Labor Force Participation Rate`** — format: Percentage (0.00%)
```
(IND) Men Labor Force Participation Rate =
-- Replace the column name below with whatever your male LFP column is named
DIVIDE(
    CALCULATE(SUM(fact_acs_wi_county[male_labor_force])),
    CALCULATE(SUM(fact_acs_wi_county[male_population])),
    0
)
```
> ⚠️ The column names above are placeholders. Use your actual column names.

---

**`(IND) Male Population Share`** — format: Percentage (0.00%)
```
(IND) Male Population Share =
DIVIDE(
    CALCULATE(SUM(fact_acs_wi_county[male_population])),
    CALCULATE(SUM(fact_acs_wi_county[total_population])),
    0
)
```
> ⚠️ Same — replace column names with your actuals.

