### 2b — Switch measures (create these on `fact_acs_wi_county`)

These are the two measures you drop into the map visuals.

**`Selected Demo Female Map`** — leave format as Auto
```
Selected Demo Female Map =
SWITCH(
    SELECTEDVALUE(dim_demo_indicator[Indicator], "Poverty Rate"),
    "Poverty Rate",              [(IND) Women Poverty Rate],
    "Labor Force Participation", [(IND) Women Labor Force Participation Rate],
    "Population Share",          [(IND) Female Population Share],
    "Poverty Gap",               [(IND) Women vs Overall Poverty Gap],
    "Homeownership",             [Homeownership Rate],
    BLANK()
)
```

---

**`Selected Demo Male Map`** — leave format as Auto
```
Selected Demo Male Map =
SWITCH(
    SELECTEDVALUE(dim_demo_indicator[Indicator], "Poverty Rate"),
    "Poverty Rate",              [(IND) Men Poverty Rate],
    "Labor Force Participation", [(IND) Men Labor Force Participation Rate],
    "Population Share",          [(IND) Male Population Share],
    "Poverty Gap",               BLANK(),
    "Homeownership",             [Homeownership Rate],
    BLANK()
)
```
> Note: Poverty Gap and some others may not have a male equivalent — those arms return BLANK() so the male map goes empty for those selections rather than showing wrong data. Remove or replace once you know what male data you have.

